.Dd September 12, 2026
.Dt SWITCHBOARDCTL 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm switchboardctl
.Nd control and inspect switchboard
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Cm status | services | reload | bundles
.Nm
.Cm start | stop | restart Ar label
.Nm
.Cm install Ar path.cap
.Nm
.Cm verify Ar path.cap ...
.Nm
.Cm deps Ar program
.Nm
.Cm recover-install Ar operation path.cap
.Nm
.Cm lifecycle status Ar root
.Nm
.Cm lifecycle query Ar root label Op Ar installation-id
.Nm
.Cm lifecycle issue Ar root
.Nm
.Cm lifecycle prune Ar root Op Ar keep-count
.Nm
.Cm lifecycle run Ar root command Op Ar argument ...
.Nm
.Cm lifecycle install | adopt Ar root source label ...
.Nm
.Cm lifecycle Ar operation root transaction source label ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is the administrative client for
.Xr switchboard 8 .
.Sh COMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width "verify path.cap ..."
.It Cm status
Show daemon and service state.
.It Cm services
List loaded service runtimes.
.It Cm reload
Transactionally rescan bundles, validate the dependency graph, and apply
additions, changes, and removals.
Requires root.
.It Cm start Ar label
Start a loaded stopped unit immediately and reset its restart backoff.
Requires root.
.It Cm stop Ar label
Gracefully stop a runtime, escalating after its configured timeout.
Requires root.
.It Cm restart Ar label
Stop the unit and then start it again, driving the same control operations as
.Cm stop
and
.Cm start .
A unit that is already stopped is simply started.
Requires root.
.It Cm install Ar path.cap
Verify and copy a bundle into
.Pa /Capabilities
as a root-owned policy tree.
Persist installation intent before publication, then commit the immutable
version reference after syncing the published directory.
An interrupted publication remains blocked until recovery.
.Ev SWITCHBOARD_LIFECYCLE_ROOT
selects an offline root and defaults to
.Pa / .
Requires root.
.It Cm verify Ar path.cap ...
Strictly validate bundle structure, manifests, executables, unique provided
names, and the combined dependency graph.
The printed effective view shows activation and local descriptors.
.It Cm deps Ar program
Inspect an ELF program and print an advisory
.Va descriptors
object for linked FileSystemCmp, NetworkCmp, and CryptoCmp clients.
Global service libraries require no manifest declaration and are ignored.
.It Cm recover-install Ar operation path.cap
Finish an interrupted bundle publication after verifying the canonical published
bundle and its recorded operation and source reference.
Requires root.
.It Cm lifecycle status Ar root
Inspect the durable installation ledger without contacting a daemon.
Owner phases are 1 (active), 2 (prepared), 3 (retired), 4 (complete),
and 5 (installing).
Delivery phases are 0 (pending) and 1 (provider acknowledged).
Records identify operation IDs, source references, readable source names,
and possible providers.
.It Cm lifecycle query Ar root label Op Ar installation-id
Query the installation authority without modifying its records.
Omit the installation ID to inspect the latest recorded installation of a label.
Supply the ID to distinguish a removed installation from its replacement.
The result is unknown, installed, installing, removing, or removed, followed
by live and staged source counts.
Unknown means no matching record; an unavailable or corrupt authority
is an error.
Neither result grants permission to delete data.
Removal describes installation state, not completion of provider cleanup.
Removal transactions do not schedule provider cleanup.
Switchboard separately schedules cleanup after committed removal.
A concurrent writer makes a query fail promptly with a busy error; retry later.
.It Cm lifecycle cleanup Ar root Op Ar label Op Ar installation-id
Inspect private-resource cleanup without modifying the authority or contacting
a daemon.
With no label, list removed or removing installations.
A label alone selects its latest installation;
supply the saved ID to inspect an older one.
The output distinguishes removal-pending, dispatch-pending, providers-pending,
and complete, and lists pending or acknowledged provider deliveries.
An active or installing identity reports not-requested.
Exit status 75 means work remains or a concurrent writer holds
the registry lock;
retry a busy query.
Exit status 66 means the selected identity is unknown.
Completion means each targeted provider has acknowledged its retention policy;
it does not mean all application-related bytes have been erased.
.It Cm lifecycle issue Ar root
Persist and print a fresh 32-digit hexadecimal operation ID for a manual
transaction.
The managed command wrapper and normal installers issue IDs automatically.
.It Cm lifecycle prune Ar root Op Ar keep-count
Discard older operational history, keeping the most recent issued transactions.
The count is 1 through 256 and defaults to 256 for this invocation.
Automatic collection uses 256; unused issued IDs are collected above 512.
Pending transactions and cleanup, live references, their dependencies, and
one last-known installation per label are preserved.
Expired exact-identity queries return unknown.
After pruning, new transactions require an authority-issued ID; expired retries
fail rather than targeting a replacement installation.
.It Cm lifecycle run Ar root command Op Ar argument ...
Run a managed package command with a fresh operation ID and selected root in
.Ev SWITCHBOARD_LIFECYCLE_OPERATION
and
.Ev SWITCHBOARD_LIFECYCLE_ROOT .
Print the operation ID and propagate the command's exit status.
The command must supply its own package root options.
A pkg invocation requires the installed lifecycle helper.
An unfinished ledger operation returns exit status 75 even if pkg returns zero.
The wrapper serializes cooperating invocations but does not roll back pkg files.
.It Cm lifecycle install | adopt Ar root source label ...
Record an already-published source, retaining an active installation's identity.
.Cm adopt
preserves legacy resource ownership when first recording an existing
installation, recording the supplied source.
This is an explicit migration action after inspecting installed files and
package state; service startup and client connections never adopt
missing labels.
Register older installations before restarting a manager that requires existing
installation records.
The runtime package registers the ambient principal
.Li org.5bsd.user-session ;
manual migration uses source
.Li pkg:runtime/runtime .
Managed upgrades preserve active installation IDs.
Use the normal bundle installer for new bundle publication.
.It Cm lifecycle Ar operation root transaction source label ...
Stage, complete, or cancel an exact installation or removal transaction.
Operations are
.Cm begin-install , begin-adopt , finish-install , cancel-install ,
.Cm prepare , retire ,
and
.Cm cancel .
A transaction is a nonzero 32-digit hexadecimal operation ID obtained from
.Cm lifecycle issue
or the managed wrapper.
A source identifies a package slot or immutable bundle version.
All labels in an invocation commit together.
Completion always addresses the recorded installation, including on retries.
Removing the last source reference records the installation as removed.
Switchboard queues private-resource cleanup separately after this durable fact.
.Pp
An interrupted operation stays pending until explicitly finished or cancelled.
Inspect actual package/file state before recovery.
.Cm finish-install
attests successful publication; prefer
.Cm recover-install
for bundles.
Cancel removal only when the source remains intact.
Success from
.Cm retire
means the removal is durably recorded; it does not attest to data deletion.
All lifecycle operations require root.
The legacy label-only reclaim endpoint is unsupported.
.It Cm bundles
List bundles installed in
.Pa /Capabilities/System
and
.Pa /Capabilities .
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# switchboardctl verify /path/to/MyApp.cap
# switchboardctl install /path/to/MyApp.cap
# switchboardctl reload
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr mac_capability 4 ,
.Xr switchboard 5 ,
.Xr switchboard 8
